On Friday, November 7, 2014 7:02:34 PM UTC-5, Janis wrote:
> Never say "It moves only reluctantly"
> => no more BUC-ID by pet?

Someone on reddit misinterpreted this the same way, but
no, the bug was more related to the word "it":  there were
two codepaths for deciding whether you could see the pet
move onto the object or not, and they were not consistent
with one another.  

In some cases the code that was deciding whether to
show the message was deciding that yes, you could see 
it, the message should be shown; but the code that was
deciding whether to be specific about the pet decided
that no, you couldn't see it, so it should just be "it".

The fix makes the two code paths consistent, so now either
you can see the pet move, and you get "Your cat moves only
reluctantly" or "Slinky moves only reluctantly" or whatever,
or else you can't see the pet move and get no message.

